  <data name="HowToPlay_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>How to play</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HowToPlay_RuleA" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The captain will start the first turn by selecting a card from their hand.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HowToPlay_RuleB" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Then, the next player in clockwise order must play a card of the same suit (if they have one), a card of another suit if they do not have the lead suit, or their king card.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HowToPlay_RuleC" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Step b will be repeated until the last player is reached.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HowToPlay_RuleD" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The player who played the highest numbered card of the lead suit will win the trick.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HowToPlay_RuleD_Sub1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>King cards beat any non-king card. They will only lose to another king card according to hierarchy (spades -&gt; hearts -&gt; clubs -&gt; diamonds).</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HowToPlay_RuleE" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The cards won by the player will be moved to their side and cannot be played again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HowToPlay_RuleF" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The number of tricks played equals the number of cards each player holds (for 3 players, 13 tricks are played). Unless all objectives are completed or one fails; if this happens, the game proceeds to the next mission or restarts it, respectively.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HowToPlay_RuleG" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Communication tokens allow players to reveal a card from their hand by placing the token on their card. Tokens cannot be placed unless one of the conditions described below is met. Depending on where it is placed, it means:</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HowToPlay_RuleG_Sub1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>If the token is placed at the top of the card, it means it is the player's highest card of that suit.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HowToPlay_RuleG_Sub2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>If the token is placed in the center of the card, it means it is the player's only card of that suit.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HowToPlay_RuleG_Sub3" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>If the token is placed at the bottom of the card, it means it is the player's lowest card of that suit.</value>
  </data>
